| Feature              | Django                            | FastAPI                              |
| -------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Main purpose         | Full web applications             | APIs and backend services            |
| Built-in admin panel | ✅ Yes                             | ❌ No                                 |
| Database ORM         | ✅ Built-in                        | Optional                             |
| User authentication  | ✅ Built-in support                | Usually added separately             |
| API development      | ✅ Yes                             | ⭐ Excellent                          |
| Performance          | Good                              | Very fast                            |
| Best for             | Complete database-driven websites | AI APIs, microservices, backend APIs |


==========

In your College AI Assistant

You currently use:

HTML + CSS + JavaScript
          ↓
       FastAPI
          ↓
       Vertex AI
          ↓
Fine-Tuned Gemini 2.5 Flash

This is a good architecture for an AI chatbot.

If you were building a complete college management system with student accounts, faculty accounts, admissions, courses, payments, databases, and an admin dashboard, Django could be a strong choice.

======

Simple way to remember

Django = Full web application framework 🏢
FastAPI = Fast API/backend framework ⚡

Both use Python, and both can also be containerized with Docker and deployed to Google Cloud Run.

Django is a strong choice for a complete college management system because 
its built-in models, authentication, admin panel, and URL structure work together in one framework, while FastAPI is better suited to focused APIs such as your AI assistant.

